---
title: Adding a new specimen record
sidebar:
  label: Adding records
  order: 2
---

{% steps %}
1. Navigate to the specimen page using the bottom navigation bar.

2. Click the `+` button to add a new specimen record.

    You can also use the three-dot menu and choose a duplicate action when you
    want to reuse part of the current specimen record.

    {% aside type="tip" %}

    If you collect the same `Specimen part` for each new specimen, use
    `Duplicate part` to minimize repetitive entry. Review the copied part before
    saving because part-level IDs, timing, and treatments should still match the
    new specimen.

    {% /aside %}

3. Select `Cataloger`.

    This is the person responsible for cataloging the specimen. Depending on the
    project field ID mode, NAHPU can use the cataloger's field number or a
    project-level field number.

4. Select `Preparator`.

    NAHPU defaults the preparator to the cataloger. If a different person
    prepares the voucher or part, update the preparator field.

5. Select the `Taxon`.

    Start typing to search the project's taxon registry, then select the
    matching record from the list. NAHPU populates the `Taxon Info` panel from
    that taxon record. Because the registry holds records at any rank, material
    that is not yet identified to species can be linked to its family or genus
    and refined later.

6. Select `ID Confidence`.

    This tells later reviewers how confident you are in the identification and
    helps curators prioritize records that need review. The values are `Low`,
    `Medium`, and `High`.

7. Select the specimen `Condition`.

    The default values are `Freshly euthanized`, `Good`, `Fair`, `Poor`,
    `Rotten`, `Released`, and `Unknown`. Conditions are a controlled
    vocabulary: edit the list in `Settings` > `Specimens` > `Conditions`.

8. Add the `Collection date`, `Collection time`, `Prep. date`, and `Prep. time`
   when available.

{% /steps %}
